WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
One matched pilot pair. The same SO-101 arm
ran one trial, then the other.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.950 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
Both saw cameras and joint readings.
Only the right could use Python.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.150 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
Aim within 15 mm and 15°.
Release and stay clear for 3 s.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.180 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
Gold is Fable, blue Python, green the arm.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.950 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
On the right, Fable draws a 20-pixel grid
on its first camera image.

6
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.180 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
Fable sends Python’s five angles
to the arm.

7
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.320 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
The right arm’s first move finished at 2:24.

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.700 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
The right wrist camera shows the jaws
closing on the carton.

9
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:37.680 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
The right arm lifts the carton,
carries it over the tray and lets go.

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.750 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
At 4:49, the right run ends.
At 4:50, the left arm’s first move returns.

11
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.500 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
The left gripper picks up its carton
and carries it over the tray.

12
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.970 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
The left gripper opens and backs away.

13
00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:59.567 line:39% position:50% size:91% align:center
Without Python, 3.1 mm and 5.0°.
With Python, 4.5 mm and 4.5°. Both pass.
